WEBVTT

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.266
AG: So what exactly is authenticity?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.374
It seems like there are about as many
variations on the concept

00:04:04.398 --> 00:04:06.152
as there are people who use it.

00:04:06.724 --> 00:04:10.546
Here's what it doesn't mean --
being a fake or a phony.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.720
It's being genuine.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.659
As a psychologist,

00:04:13.683 --> 00:04:16.270
I think about authenticity
as erasing the gap

00:04:16.294 --> 00:04:19.065
between what you
think and feel on the inside

00:04:19.089 --> 00:04:21.210
and what you share on the outside.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:24.116
And that can apply
in a few different realms --

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:25.996
sharing your genuine feelings,

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:27.262
your opinions

00:04:27.286 --> 00:04:28.498
and your ideas.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.726
Look, there's good reason
to value authenticity.